# HackMyAgent scanner exemptions. Keep this file as small as possible.
# Format: one rule per line. Bare path patterns exempt the path from all checks;
# `!CHECK-ID` lines exempt one check globally. Parser: `src/hardening/scanner.ts` (loadHmaIgnore)
# in the hackmyagent repo.
#
# The four paths below are conformance test vectors: fixture credentials, their
# Ed25519 signatures, canonical byte strings and their SHA-256 digests. Every
# value in them is a published, deterministic test input — the whole point of the
# suite is that anyone can reproduce them — so a credential detector reading them
# reports the artifact's subject matter, not an exposure (measured 2026-08-24:
# AST-CRED-003 fired on the label `"fixtureType": "atx-credential"` in
# conformance.json, a type name with no value beside it; AST-CRED-001 fired on a
# canonicalization vector's hex/digest). Exempting the paths rather than the
# checks keeps hand-maintained source and workflows under the credential rules.
# The exemption is safe because these paths are GENERATED (scripts/generate-fixtures)
# and byte-pinned in CI (conformance.yml "Fixture byte-pin"): nothing lands here
# by hand, and a regeneration that changed them fails the pin.
fixtures/
vectors/
jcs-vectors/vectors/
conformance.json
